  "question": {
    "text": "A particle moving along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis has acceleration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>,&nbsp;at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> given by<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> are constants. The particle at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and the instant when&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the particle&#39;s velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></math> is"
  },
